1.16.1: the sample photos travel with the source

The six sample photographs (the author's own, CC BY 4.0) and their
manifest are now tracked in git and ship in every tarball. Since 0.9.0
they had been ignored and lived only in working trees and on gh-pages,
so a fresh clone - the MacBook, the sandbox - had none, and a release
from such a tree published a strip with captions and no pictures.
.gitignore keeps *.jpg but un-ignores web/samples/*.jpg and *.json;
release.sh drops the old web/samples/ rule from an existing checkout
and adds the photos on import.

Both gh-pages deploys (release and --restage) now go through one
deploy_pages function using the orphan-branch sequence: the staging
tree is emptied with git rm first, which removes .gitignore from it,
so main's *.jpg rule can no longer swallow the photos - the --restage
path had branched from main and did exactly that. The function refuses
to publish if fewer than twelve sample jpgs are staged, and cleans up
its worktree on failure. The restage also no longer copies the source
tree onto gh-pages.

.gitignore consolidated: *.d, /superjuice and /tests/test_web_shim
grouped with the other build products.
